 "final_result": "NaCl band-structure workflow completed successfully.\n\nMaterials Project ID: mp-22862 (space group Fm-3m, #225).\nAtom count: 2 atoms before and after primitive-cell reduction (NaCl is already primitive in the Fm-3m setting).\n\nWorkflow outline:\n1. Fetched NaCl base CIF from Materials Project (mp-22862, Fm-3m #225), reduced to primitive cell (2 atoms: Na, Cl).\n2. generate_structures.py: wrote 51 structures (structure_000 unperturbed + 50 perturbed with T=300 K thermal displacements, U_Na=0.006 A^2, U_Cl=0.004 A^2, plus 0.1% random lattice strain).\n3. Fetched Pseudo-Dojo pseudopotentials (NC, PBESOL, stringent, scalar-relativistic): Na.upf (z_valence=9, 44.0 Ha), Cl.upf (z_valence=7, 29.0 Ha).\n4. setup_jobs.py: created calculations/000-050/ with pw.in (SCF, ecutwfc=88.0 Ry, ecutrho=352.0 Ry, occupations=fixed, conv_thr=1e-8, kpts=8x8x8), bands.in (nbnd=16, kpts from kpath), bands_post.in (lsym=.false.), kpath.json, and pseudopotentials.\n5. run_espresso_workflow on calculations/000: success (scf=3.6s, bands_scf=14.7s, bands_post=2.8s).\n6. plot_bands.py: plotted band structure aligned to VBM, saved calculations/000/bands_000.pdf.\n\nASE functions used: ase.io.read/write (CIF I/O), ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in (QE input generation), ase.Atoms (structure representation).\n\nBand gap obtained: 5.04 eV (VBM=1.215 eV, CBM=6.255 eV, aligned to VBM). This is consistent with the experimental NaCl gap of ~8.9 eV being underestimated by DFT (PBESOL typically underestimates gaps by ~30-40%).\n\nScientific assumptions:\n- Scalar-relativistic pseudopotentials (Z<54 for both Na and Cl, no spin-orbit needed).\n- occupations='fixed' (NaCl is a clear insulator with ~5 eV gap).\n- T=300 K for thermal displacements (NaCl stable at room temperature, melting point ~1074 K).\n- ecutwfc=88.0 Ry (44.0 Ha * 2, from Na pseudopotential -- the larger of the two).\n- nbnd=16 (2x occupied bands; total valence electrons = 9+7 = 16, occupied = 8).\n\nItems for expert review:\n- The DFT band gap (5.04 eV) is lower than the experimental value (~8.9 eV), which is expected for PBESOL. A hybrid functional (HSE06) or GW correction would be needed for quantitative agreement.\n- The k-point mesh (8x8x8) was chosen by scf_kmesh for an insulator; convergence testing would be advisable for production calculations.",
